---
import Information from '../layouts/Information.astro';
const commentsEnabled = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_COMMENTS_ENABLED === 'true';
const contents = [
  {id:'information',label:'Information and forms'}, {id:'use',label:'How information is used'},
  ...(commentsEnabled ? [{ id: 'song-discussion', label: 'Public song discussion' }] : []),
  {id:'storage',label:'Cookies and browser storage'}, {id:'services',label:'Services and external links'},
  {id:'retention',label:'Retention and your choices'}, {id:'security',label:'Security'},
  {id:'changes',label:'Changes'}, {id:'contact',label:'Privacy questions'},
];
---
<Information title="Privacy Policy" description="What the current Keertana site does with form details, browser storage, and requests to external services." policy updatedAt="2026-10-17" contents={contents}>
  <section id="information" aria-labelledby="information-heading"><h2 id="information-heading">Information and forms</h2>
    <p>You can browse Keertana without an account. There is no account database, login, payment system, advertising integration, or external error-reporting service configured in the application. Vercel Web Analytics is included in production builds to understand site traffic.</p>
    <p>Contribution forms ask for the following details:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Submit a Song:</strong> title, language, lyrics, and an acknowledgement; optional Roman title, alternate title, author/composer, source/reference, category, notes, contributor name, and email.</li>
      <li><strong>Report an Error:</strong> the selected song, issue type, and description; optional suggested correction, contributor name, and email. Reports opened from a song include its title, identifier, and language.</li>
      <li><strong>Join the Team:</strong> name, email, and interests; optional skills/experience, motivation, and portfolio, GitHub, or website link.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>These forms validate details and prepare email drafts in your browser.</strong> The site does not send automatically or save form details to local storage or a site database. If you open the email draft, its details are passed to your chosen email application; you review and press Send there. You can instead copy the message into webmail. A browser may restore fields or supply autofill according to its settings.</p>
    <p>Opening a page makes a request to the server delivering it. Technical request information can include your IP address, browser information, requested address, and time of access. The production host’s settings and retention need owner confirmation.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="use" aria-labelledby="use-heading"><h2 id="use-heading">How information is used</h2>
    <p>Form details are used locally to check required fields and formats and prepare an email. Messages you choose to send to keertanasongs@gmail.com can be read for corrections, contribution review and replies. Email can include the form details, your sender address and other information you include. No separate form provider or CMS is connected.</p>
    <p>Browser storage supports returning to saved or recent songs and remembering display preferences. Search matches titles against an index downloaded from this site. Typed search terms are processed in the browser; the current search interface does not send them to an external search service or save them as search history.</p>
    <p>Copying lyrics writes them to your clipboard when you choose Copy. Sharing uses your device’s share feature, where available, or copies the song URL. The destination you choose may handle the shared information under its own practices.</p>
    {!commentsEnabled && <p>The song-discussion preview is an inactive demonstration. Its fields cannot accept or send information. Visits to the preview and the separate interest-confirmation page are included in ordinary production page-view analytics to understand demand. Choosing the interest link does not submit a comment or create a subscription.</p>}
  </section>
  <section id="storage" aria-labelledby="storage-heading"><h2 id="storage-heading">Cookies and browser storage</h2>
    <p>Cookies use the browser’s cookie mechanism and can accompany requests to a website. Local storage is a separate browser store; Keertana’s saved library is not a cookie and is not automatically sent with page requests.</p>
    <p>Keertana does not set authentication or advertising cookies. Vercel Web Analytics uses a daily visitor hash rather than cookies. This does not describe cookies that a deployed host or its protection settings might add. Browser-local saved songs and preferences use local storage.</p>
    <dl class="information-storage">
      <div><dt>Saved Songs and Recently Viewed</dt><dd>Local storage keeps song identifiers in this browser. Saved songs remain until removed or cleared. Recent visits are deduplicated, ordered with the newest first, and limited to eight; older entries are replaced. Lyrics and contributor details are not copied into this store. There is no account-based synchronization.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Display preferences</dt><dd>Local storage remembers a chosen light/dark theme and lyric font size. These are preferences for this browser, not a user profile.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Offline cache</dt><dd>A service worker uses browser Cache Storage for the home and offline pages, search index, and visited same-site pages and resources. Cached pages can remain available offline and may briefly show an older version while refreshing. This is separate from cookies and local storage.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>
  {commentsEnabled && <section id="song-discussion" aria-labelledby="song-discussion-heading"><h2 id="song-discussion-heading">Public song discussion</h2>
    <p>When you choose to view a song’s discussion, the browser contacts Keertana’s Supabase comments service for approved comments. Opening the comment form also loads Cloudflare Turnstile to check submissions for spam. These providers can receive technical request information, including your IP address and browser information, under their own policies. See <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" rel="external">Supabase’s Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="external">Cloudflare’s Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
    <p>The comment form asks for a display name, a short comment, an optional HTTPS reference link, and confirmation that approved content may be public. No commenter account or email is requested. Submission sends those details, the song identifier, a request identifier used to avoid duplicate retries, and a spam-check token to the server. Keertana’s comment table does not include an IP address or email field.</p>
    <p>Accepted comments are stored as pending for owner review. Only approved display names, comment text, reference links, publication dates, and public comment identifiers are returned to visitors. Pending and rejected comments and moderation notes are not publicly displayed. The owner can approve, reject, or remove entries in the secured moderation dashboard. Publication and a moderation response time are not guaranteed.</p>
    <p>Your draft is kept only in the current form and is not saved to browser storage by this feature. Accepted submissions are stored in the Supabase database. No automatic deletion schedule is configured; the owner reviews retention and deletion separately. To request removal of a published comment, contact <a href="mailto:keertanasongs@gmail.com">keertanasongs@gmail.com</a> with the song link and enough details to identify the entry. Approved comments can be read or copied by others while public.</p>
  </section>}
  <section id="services" aria-labelledby="services-heading"><h2 id="services-heading">Services and external links</h2>
    <p>The Latin font, Inter, is requested from Google Fonts. These requests connect to Google’s font servers and expose your IP address and request information needed to deliver the font. See <a href="https://fonts.googleblog.com/2022/11/your-privacy-and-google-fonts.html" rel="external">Google’s font-service privacy explanation</a>. Telugu and Devanagari fonts are bundled with Keertana and served with the site.</p>
    <p>The project’s default public address is on Vercel, but the active production hosting settings and enabled services have not been verified. If delivered through Vercel, that provider handles request information under its <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" rel="external">Privacy Notice</a>. The owner must confirm the actual provider, logs, retention, and any dashboard-enabled analytics or protection before launch.</p>
    <p><strong>Vercel Web Analytics:</strong> when enabled for the deployed project, the production site sends page-view information to Vercel for aggregated traffic statistics. This can include page URLs, referrers, filtered query parameters, timestamps, approximate location, and device, operating-system and browser information. Vercel describes this service as cookie-free, with a visitor hash that resets daily. Keertana does not configure custom events to send contribution fields, saved-song lists, or typed search terms. See <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" rel="external">Vercel's analytics privacy documentation</a>.</p>
    <p>No embedded media, external song API or advertising service is configured in the application. An external policy or other website link takes you to a service with its own privacy practices.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="retention" aria-labelledby="retention-heading"><h2 id="retention-heading">Retention and your choices</h2>
    <p>Local storage has no expiry set by Keertana. It remains until cleared by you or your browser, replaced, or removed by the application. You can remove an individual saved song with its Saved button. Clear Keertana’s site data in browser settings to remove the saved library, recent visits, preferences, and offline cache; this also removes offline availability until resources are downloaded again.</p>
    <p>Browser storage belongs to a browser profile and site address. Different devices, browsers, or addresses do not share it. Private browsing and storage restrictions may limit persistence. Other people using the same browser profile may see its saved and recent songs.</p>
    <p>Emails you send are stored in the receiving Gmail account, separately from the site and your browser storage. No automatic deletion schedule is configured by the website. Your email provider may also store sent messages and drafts. Google's handling is described in its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="external">Privacy Policy</a>. Do not rely on the form as a saved draft: navigating away can discard it.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="security" aria-labelledby="security-heading"><h2 id="security-heading">Security</h2>
    <p>No website or browser store can promise absolute security. Avoid entering passwords, financial details, or other sensitive information in contribution fields. {commentsEnabled ? 'The comments store is separate from email contribution forms; removal requests are handled by the owner, and there is no self-service deletion portal.' : 'This version has no server-side submission store or deletion portal. Adding a receiver will require reviewing how information is secured, accessed, and retained before enabling it.'}</p>
  </section>
  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-heading"><h2 id="changes-heading">Changes to this page</h2>
    <p>This page will be updated when the site's services or data practices change. The date above identifies the last update; it does not certify legal compliance.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-heading"><h2 id="contact-heading">Privacy questions</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, email <a href="mailto:keertanasongs@gmail.com">keertanasongs@gmail.com</a>. The <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> also lists contribution options.</p>
  </section>
</Information>
